+// whatever the button set. So as the guest boots, the window sets
+// USER_ROTATION to |userRotation| (what goes with hw.initialOrientation) as
+// soon as Android's settings service answers, before the lock screen shows: it
+// waits for adbd, then tries every quarter second for up to a minute. It turns
+// nothing: the window is at that orientation already, and so is Android
+// unless the button left it otherwise. The adb arguments.
+std::vector<std::string> bootUserRotationArgs(int userRotation);
